    <section xml:id="payload" xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
    <title xml:id="payload.title">Self-authenticating BACAP payload</title>
    <para>The first message sent, the <code>VoucherPayload</code>, is authenticated in the following
        manner: </para>

            <orderedlist>
              <listitem>
                <para>The <code>VoucherPayload</code> is computed. </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>A cryptographic hash of the <code>VoucherPayload</code> is computed. This hash
              <emphasis role="strong">is</emphasis> the <emphasis>Voucher</emphasis>.</para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>The <emphasis role="strong">Voucher</emphasis> is used to derive a BACAP
            read/write capability set. </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>The <code>VoucherPayload</code> is uploaded to the BACAP sequence described by
            the capability (at index 0). </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>Anyone who intercepts the <emphasis role="strong">Voucher</emphasis> can read
              <emphasis role="strong">and</emphasis> write the sequence. </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>But: Since the <emphasis role="strong">Voucher</emphasis> is a hash over the
              <code>VoucherPayload</code>, writing the sequence with anything but the
              <code>VoucherPayload</code> will be detectable by the recipient. </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>This means that the contents <emphasis>cannot</emphasis> be modified
            undetectably by the interceptor. </para>
              </listitem>
            </orderedlist>
  </section>
</section></section>
